# Design tokens — one namespace, three consumers

Every color, font, radius, spacing and text-size value a component uses must
resolve to one of these tokens. Never a raw hex value, never an undefined CSS
variable. This three-way binding — one value, three places it's consumed — is
the single highest-leverage fix versus the old build, where 30 registered
tokens pointed at CSS variables that didn't exist anywhere.

```
src/app/globals.css        :root { --fn-color-primary: #1B3A2F; ... }
        ↓ (@theme inline block, Tailwind v4 CSS-first config)
Tailwind utilities          bg-primary, text-primary, font-display, text-lg, rounded-md, ...
        ↓
src/builder-registry.ts     editor.settings.designTokens — var(--fn-*, fallback)
```

Change a value in `globals.css` and the app, the Tailwind utility classes, and
the Builder token picker all move together. There is no `tailwind.config.ts`
— Tailwind 4 is CSS-first; the `@theme inline` block in `globals.css` is the
only place the Tailwind side of this binding lives.

## The token list

| Token | Value | Tailwind utility |
|---|---|---|
| `--fn-color-primary` | `#1B3A2F` (deep forest) | `bg-primary` / `text-primary` |
| `--fn-color-accent` | `#D4622A` (trail orange) | `bg-accent` / `text-accent` |
| `--fn-color-sand` | `#E8DFD2` | `bg-sand` / `text-sand` |
| `--fn-color-ink` | `#14161A` (text) | `bg-ink` / `text-ink` |
| `--fn-color-slate` | `#5C6670` (muted text) | `bg-slate` / `text-slate` |
| `--fn-color-surface` | `#FFFFFF` | `bg-surface` / `text-surface` |
| `--fn-color-surface-alt` | `#F7F5F1` | `bg-surface-alt` |
| `--fn-color-success` | `#2F6B4F` | `bg-success` / `text-success` |
| `--fn-color-warning` | `#B8791C` | `bg-warning` / `text-warning` |
| `--fn-color-danger` | `#A6342B` | `bg-danger` / `text-danger` |
| `--fn-font-display` | Instrument Sans (`next/font`) | `font-display` |
| `--fn-font-body` | Inter (`next/font`) | `font-body` |
| `--fn-radius-sm/md/lg` | 4 / 8 / 16px | `rounded-sm/md/lg` |
| `--fn-text-xs…4xl` | 12 / 14 / 16 / 18 / 24 / 32 / 44 / 56px | `text-xs…4xl` |

Spacing has **no** `--fn-space-*` override: the seed spec's scale
(4/8/12/16/24/32/48/64px) already equals Tailwind's default rem scale at steps
1/2/3/4/6/8/12/16 — `p-4` already is 16px, `gap-6` already is 24px. Don't
invent a parallel spacing token; use Tailwind's built-in spacing scale as-is.

Any color/font/size a new component needs that isn't in this list should be
added to `globals.css` (`:root` and the `@theme inline` block) and to
`editor.settings.designTokens` in `src/builder-registry.ts` — all three, every
time. Adding it to only one or two silently breaks the binding this file
exists to protect.

## Editor strictness

`editor.settings` is currently `styleStrictMode: true, allowOverridingTokens:
false` — the Style tab only offers these tokens, no arbitrary values. That's
deliberate (the SiteOne/Al Tayer "token tiering" guardrail demo) — don't
loosen it per-component. If a specific component genuinely needs an escape
hatch, that's a space-wide settings conversation, not a per-component
registration option.
